course: dictionary
lesson: 4078
title: Germinate: when seeds start to grow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A seed is a tiny package with a little food stored inside it. When it has the right conditions, it wakes up. Germinate means the seed starts to grow: a root goes down into the soil and a shoot pushes up. «Most seeds do not need light to germinate, because they use their own food store at first.» So the seed does not need sunshine to begin.
explain: Context helps here. The sentence says seeds use their own food store, so germinate must be about starting to grow, not about shining or changing colour. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «Most seeds do not need light to start to grow» still makes sense.
explain: «Most seeds need warmth as well as water and air to germinate.» Here the clues are warmth, water and air. Seeds need all three to begin growing. Germinate can also be used for ideas. To germinate an idea means to begin to develop it, but this is a formal use, so you will meet it mostly in writing.
fact: Germinate is a verb. Its other forms are germinates, germinated and germinating.
fact: When a seed germinates, it puts out a root and a shoot.
fact: «Seeds germinate» and «take days to germinate» are common phrases in science.
fact: Seeds usually need water, warmth and air to germinate. Light is not needed at first.
fact: «Germinate» can also mean to begin to develop an idea. This is a formal meaning.
exercise: «Most seeds do not need light to germinate.» What does germinate mean in this sentence? | To turn into a flower | * To start to grow, with a root and a shoot | To dry out and crumble | To be eaten by birds
exercise: Maya says a seed needs light to germinate. Is she right? | Yes, seeds only germinate in the dark | Yes, light is the most important thing | * No, most seeds do not need light at first, because they use their own food store | No, seeds never need water
exercise: «Most seeds need warmth as well as water and air to germinate.» Which of these does a seed need, besides water and air, to germinate? | Sand | * Warmth | Light | Sugar
test: Ella's beans will ___ in the jar by Friday. | germinating | germinated | germinates | * germinate
test: In science, Sam puts beans on wet cotton wool to see them ___. | slide | sparkle | * germinate | disappear
exam: «The idea began to germinate in her mind.» What does germinate mean here? | * Began to develop | Was forgotten | Died away | Was painted
